Rejecting the investigation's findings, the group said a technical committee “found no tampering with the oil pipelines,” which it claimed, “conclusively proves the falsity of the smuggling claims.”
ERBIL, Kurdistan Region of Iraq &ndash; Iraq&rsquo;s pro-Iran Kataib Hezbollah on Sunday rejected the Iraqi government's findings in an investigation into alleged oil smuggling in Babil&rsquo;s Jurf al-Nasr, accusing Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi&rsquo;s government of using the case to pressure the group into surrendering its weapons.
Zaidi ordered the formation of a committee on Wednesday to investigate the case, following an intelligence report alleging that an oil-smuggling network had been operating in Jurf al-Nasr since 2021, in an area described as being &ldquo;under the responsibility of one of the armed factions.&rdquo;
